positions.description:
Development of the web application for conducting vibrodiagnostics of industry machines

- Implemented automatic generation of PDF and EXCEL reports (FPDF, Openpyxl, Celery), which made it possible to reduce the T2M of the report (key product metric) from 4 days to 3 hours;
- Created a service for collecting statistics on labeled data, which allowed PO and CTO to monitor the problem of lack of valid data for training ML models;
- Designed a PostgreSQL and S3 databases for the application’s services;
- Split the database when migrating from a monolithic to a microservices-based architecture;
- Implemented automated DQ checks, which allowed timely anomaly detection of in data;
- Moderated a weekly meeting of developers to discuss the implementation of features, which allowed to reduce the number of logical errors in code and estimate the time required to implement a feature more accurately during planning;
- Conducted technical discovery to optimize the application and timely refactoring.

Development of business intelligent solutions for Rich Communication Services (5,5MM customers)

- Implemented the creation of optimized data marts (DAU, MAU...) and ad-hoc reports;
- Automated ETL processes for transferring data between Data Lake layers and generating client reporting by writing AirFlow dags.

Constructing a roadster

- Studied the behavior of the car in an accident by simulating collisions in SolidWorks and NX Siemens;
- Designed and conducted research on the frame, rims, and retractable roof strength by simulating loads from a person’s weight to accidents in NX.

Constructing a Formula Student bolid

- Designed and carried out strength calculations of an aero-dynamic system for Formula student bolid by simulating air flows in Ansys and SolidWorks;
- Led a team of 7 members and managed the development of 3 types of wings, which allowed designing front and back wings that create an optimum downforce at their minimum weight.
